---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { catalog } from '../lib/cre';
import { niches } from '../lib/niches';
---
<Base title="About" description="What LexJolt is, what it will not do, and how the numbers are made.">
  <div class="lexjolt-shell lj-page" style="max-width:760px">
    <p class="lexjolt-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="lexjolt-h1">Tools that show their working</h1>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      LexJolt is a set of free tools for people who make property decisions and content about them.
      There is no account, no email wall, and no sales call. Nothing you type is sent anywhere: the
      calculators run in your browser.
    </p>

    <hr class="lj-hr" />

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2">What is here</h2>
    <ul class="lj-list">
      <li><a href="/calculators">{catalog.calculators.length} calculators</a><span class="lj-sub">Valuation, financing, income, returns, tax, commercial, market. Each one shows its inputs and recomputes as you type.</span></li>
      <li><a href="/niches">{niches.length} measured niches</a><span class="lj-sub">Scored on six weighted dimensions from real search results, with the rules published and the arithmetic visible.</span></li>
      <li><a href="/ideas">An idea studio</a><span class="lj-sub">Short-video ideas that each name the calculator or niche behind them.</span></li>
      <li><a href="/videos">A video per calculator</a><span class="lj-sub">1080×1920, rendered from the same engine, transcript on every card.</span></li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="lj-hr" />

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2">What it will not do</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      It will not tell you a deal is good. Every default is a worked example chosen to make the
      arithmetic legible, not a recommendation. It will not price your market for you: the assumptions
      are inputs, and the answer is only as good as what you put in. It will not pretend a measurement
      is a prediction — the niche scores describe what the search results looked like when they were
      read, and search results move.
    </p>

    <hr class="lj-hr" />

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2">How the numbers are made</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      The calculators are ported from a Python engine and gated on golden vectors: every calculator has
      three recorded input/output pairs produced by the Python implementation, and the TypeScript port
      must reproduce all of them within 1e-9 before the site is allowed to build. A formula that drifts
      fails the build, not the user.
    </p>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm" style="margin-top:12px">
      The niche numbers come from reading the top results of two search phrases per niche, then
      computing medians per phrase and combining by median rather than pooling — two phrases can be two
      different topics, and pooling one weak phrase into a strong niche hides the difference.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:24px"><a href="/contact">Say something about a number →</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
